{"content":"Excellent. Now I have all the information. Let me provide the complete answer:\n\nq20.\n\n**Mechanism:** Server-Sent Events (SSE) via HTTP text/event-stream protocol with Bearer token authentication. The server broadcasts JSON-serialized events through an in-memory hub with per-client buffered channels (32-event capacity) and heartbeat pings every 30 seconds.\n\n**Hub path:** `server/router/api/v1/sse_hub.go` (type `SSEHub`, methods `Subscribe()`, `Broadcast()`, `Unsubscribe()`, `Close()`)\n\n**Handler names (memo service methods that broadcast through the hub):**\n- `CreateMemo()` — broadcasts `SSEEventMemoCreated` events (line 163)\n- `DeleteMemo()` — broadcasts `SSEEventMemoDeleted` events (line 585)\n- `CreateMemoComment()` — broadcasts `SSEEventMemoCommentCreated` events (line 126)\n- `dispatchMemoUpdatedSideEffects()` — broadcasts `SSEEventMemoUpdated` events (line 71)\n- `UpsertMemoReaction()` — broadcasts `SSEEventReactionUpserted` events (line 106)\n- `DeleteMemoReaction()` — broadcasts `SSEEventReactionDeleted` events (line 161)\n\nAll broadcasts are filtered server-side by visibility (Private events visible only to creator/admin) before being sent to subscribers. The endpoint is at `/api/v1/sse`.","iteration":10,"turn":1,"type":"assistant"}
